The {{Term/Store|Lynel Mask||Series, BotW, TotK, AoC}} is a recurring [[Item]]} in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK, AoC}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="AoC Allies"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Descriptions BotW}}
The Lynel Mask is a piece of [[Armor]] that can be purchased from [[Kilton]] at the [[Fang and Bone]] for 999 [[Mon]] shop after freeing three [[Divine Beast]]s.<ref name="BotW Kilton"/> It cannot be enhanced by a [[Great Fairy]], nor can it be [[Dye]]d at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]]. When worn, it grants [[Link]] the [[Disguise (Mechanic)|Disguise]] [[Added Effect]], allowing him to blend in with [[Lynel]]s, though they are smart enough to eventually see through his disguise and attack.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> The Lynel Mask does not prevent other [[Enemy|Enemies]] in the same area from attacking Link. It also makes quiet Lynel sounds as Link moves around. While wearing the Lynel Mask, Link adopts a new idle pose to match that of a Lynel.

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Descriptions TotK}}
The Lynel Mask returns in {{TotK|-}}, functioning the same as it did in {{BotW|-}} with the exception of the Lynels in the [[Floating Coliseum]], as they are scripted to attack [[Link]] without provocation. It can be obtained from [[Koltin's Stall]] for four [[Bubbul Gem]]s after trading a total of 33 Bubbul Gems for the prior rewards. Subsequent Lynel Masks can be purchased from [[Cece]] for 4000 [[Rupee]]s.

==Other Appearances==
==={{AoC|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
{{Descriptions AoC}}
The Lynel Mask is a piece of [[Attire]] that can only be worn by [[Link]], and is only obtained by completing the [[Quest#Hyrule Warriors: Age of Calamity|Quest]] "[[Mystery Meal for the Merchant]]". It was crafted by the [[Fang and Bone]]'s owner.<ref name="AoC Allies"/>
{{Noncanon|End}}

